# The image needs exactly one file from this repository (docker/entrypoint.sh);
# everything else it contains is downloaded and checksummed during the build.
#
# So instead of listing what to leave out (.git, .env with its password,
# .runtime/, backups/, *.tar.gz, game data ...), ignore everything and allow
# that one file back in. The build context stays a few kilobytes no matter
# what accumulates in the checkout - which also keeps `my-tes3mp deploy` fast,
# since it sends the context over SSH.
#
# (The Dockerfile itself is always sent, ignored or not.)
*
!docker/
docker/*
!docker/entrypoint.sh
